---
import { base } from '../site';

// Answers are HTML (one links to the privacy policy).
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can I export or migrate my bookmarks to another browser?', a: 'Yes. You can export your entire library or hand-pick selected bookmarks into an open JSON file at any time. When you install XMarks on another browser or machine (Chrome, Brave, Edge), click Import to restore everything, including categories, tags and notes.' },
  { q: 'What happens if an author deletes their post on X?', a: 'Once a post is saved to XMarks, it is preserved locally in your browser. Even if the author deletes the tweet, switches their account to private, or gets suspended on X, the post text and your notes stay in your library. Images and videos are loaded from X, so those can stop showing once the post is gone.' },
  { q: 'Can I organize posts in bulk or use the keyboard?', a: 'Yes. Tick posts with their checkboxes, or select everything in view, then move them to a category, export them or delete them in one go. Shortcuts: / to search, E to edit a note, C for a new category, G then A for all bookmarks, and ? to see them all.' },
  { q: 'Does XMarks send my bookmarks to any servers?', a: `No. Everything is stored locally on your device. There is no XMarks account, no remote database and no tracking. The full details are in the <a href="${base}privacy/">privacy policy</a>.` },
  { q: 'I use more than one X account. Are my bookmarks kept separate?', a: 'They can be. By default everything goes into one library. Open the library menu in the dashboard sidebar and choose "One library per X account" and each account gets its own library, created the first time XMarks sees it. You can also add libraries yourself and pick which one new saves go to. Every library is stored in the same browser profile, so anyone who can open that profile can open all of them. To keep people apart, use separate Chrome profiles.' },
  { q: 'Does auto-categorize send my bookmarks anywhere?', a: 'No. The first time you turn it on, XMarks downloads a small model (about 45 MB) from Hugging Face. After that it runs inside your browser, and your bookmark text never leaves your device. It’s off until you turn it on.' },
  { q: 'I have thousands of bookmarks. Will sync finish?', a: 'Sync scrolls through your bookmarks on X (the Bookmarks page, or the Bookmarks tab in History) and saves as it goes. You can pause and pick up later, and posts it already has are skipped.' },
  { q: 'Does it work with X’s themes?', a: 'Yes. The save button and menus follow X’s Light, Dim and Dark themes. The dashboard has light, dark and system themes, four card densities (Ultra, Compact, Default, Spacious), and you choose where the save button sits in X’s action bar.' },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="faq container">
  <h2 class="section-title">Questions</h2>
  <dl>
    {
      faqs.map((f) => (
        <div class="item">
          <dt>{f.q}</dt>
          <dd set:html={f.a} />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    padding-top: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 380px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 56px;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .item {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  dt {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  dd :global(a) {
    color: var(--text);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .faq {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
